From: GUI_ipk maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] tun: reject non-positive TUNSETSNDBUF values

Backport the input validation present in Linux 4.1.52.  A non-positive send
buffer size is invalid and must not be propagated to the socket.

This patch intentionally changes drivers/net/tun.c only and does not alter
the networking core ABI.
---
 drivers/net/tun.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/tun.c
+++ b/drivers/net/tun.c
@@ -2015,6 +2015,10 @@ static long __tun_chr_ioctl(struct file
 			ret = -EFAULT;
 			break;
 		}
+		if (sndbuf <= 0) {
+			ret = -EINVAL;
+			break;
+		}
 
 		tun->sndbuf = sndbuf;
 		tun_set_sndbuf(tun);
